"notes": "Modified cash basis school district; School Nutrition is reported inside Other Governmental Funds, so there are no business-type funds (business_type null). Governmental lines from the Total column (p3-4); General Fund transfers out 155,000 equal transfers in to Nutrition 100,000 and Activities 55,000 so net transfers are zero in the Total column. Beginning cash = beginning fund balances (p4), ending cash = total assets/fund balance (p5). Balance sheet from the government-wide asset/net position section on p2 (primary government column; component unit Foundation excluded). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p7-10) recorded in place of the p6 combining schedule (more detailed; p6 used only for the Depreciation column and Reclassification column). Hidden transfer: p6 Reclassification column removes 65,000 from General Fund spending (plant -15,000, transportation -50,000) against the Depreciation Fund's 65,000 transfer-in (p11); recorded as contra expenditure lines plus other financing -65,000 (page does not show which lines). The 155,000 transfer is also printed as 'Transfers 8000' inside the General Fund total disbursements 7,722,480 (recorded as other financing, includes flag). Other General Fund reclassifications (categorical and federal program lines to Instruction on p6) are mapped to instruction. Budget amounts are printed at group level for several support-service headings and are only attached to lines where printed on the line. Bond Fund had no receipts or disbursements (p13, balance 55,866 unchanged) so no detail lines. Depreciation Fund and Nutrition/Activities totals as printed. Read pages 1-17 of 17"
